1
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:07,083
Now, Seras...

2
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:09,125
Take off your clothes.

3
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:12,041
Huh?

4
00:00:12,166 --> 00:00:15,208
The people of Mils saw you
in that outfit, right?

5
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:17,083
Oh...

6
00:00:17,208 --> 00:00:19,166
Sorry to give you the wrong idea.

7
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:22,041
I'll admit I was a bit shaken.

8
00:00:22,125 --> 00:00:27,125
H-Hold on a moment. When did we start
acting like our agreement is still in effect?

9
00:00:27,125 --> 00:00:29,083
I have a proposal for you.

10
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:33,083
Why don't you negotiate with the Witch
of Taboos and have her shelter you?

11
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:35,083
The Witch of Taboos?

12
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:38,125
No one has ever figured out
where she lives, right?

13
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:39,166
Indeed.

14
00:00:39,208 --> 00:00:44,041
I'm heading to the Land of Monsters myself
to learn more about that ancient script.

15
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:46,083
So our agreement's still good, no?

16
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,166
Why go so far for me?

17
00:00:49,125 --> 00:00:51,041
You remind me of someone.

18
00:00:51,125 --> 00:00:53,125
You don't look or sound very similar,

19
00:00:53,166 --> 00:00:55,208
and your personalities are different, but...

20
00:00:56,083 --> 00:00:58,083
If I had to say, you have the same aura.

21
00:00:59,041 --> 00:01:03,000
So cutting out on you here
would feel like abandoning my aunt.

22
00:01:03,041 --> 00:01:04,083
Sir Tooka...

23
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:06,125
You truly are a kind man.

24
00:01:06,125 --> 00:01:09,041
Yeah, I already know.

25
00:01:13,083 --> 00:01:15,125
Not enough to level up, huh?

26
00:01:15,166 --> 00:01:16,125
Now then...

27
00:01:19,041 --> 00:01:22,166
If you answer our questions honestly,
I'll have mercy on you.

28
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:25,166
Damn brat! Don't think you can get away
with defying the Black Dragon Knights!

29
00:01:25,208 --> 00:01:27,083
- Damn brat! Don't think you can get away
with defying the Black Dragon Knights!
- I'm not lying.

30
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:30,166
I can dismiss the nonlethal setting
and spare him from his suffering.

31
00:01:30,208 --> 00:01:33,208
Who is it that wants me dead?

32
00:01:33,208 --> 00:01:35,125
A-All right.

33
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:38,041
I'm a little curious.

34
00:01:38,041 --> 00:01:39,208
I wanna see how a former high elf princess

35
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
who swore her sword to the Holy Empire

36
00:01:42,041 --> 00:01:44,166
reacts when she learns the truth!

37
00:01:44,208 --> 00:01:45,208
Seras!

38
00:01:49,166 --> 00:01:51,125
He's currently out of range.

39
00:01:52,041 --> 00:01:54,166
No, worse yet, he'sâ€”

40
00:01:56,125 --> 00:01:58,208
Seras Ashrain.

41
00:02:00,166 --> 00:02:03,083
His garb and hair are white.

42
00:02:03,083 --> 00:02:05,083
His eyes alone are a vivid red...

43
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,166
I am Civit,

44
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,166
though many in this world
call me by another name...

45
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,083
"Humanity's Strongest."

46
00:03:47,166 --> 00:03:51,208
HUMANITY'S STRONGEST, CIVIT GARTLAND

47
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:53,208
Hand them over.

48
00:03:54,166 --> 00:04:00,000
Surrender to me your nation's strongest.

49
00:04:08,208 --> 00:04:10,166
Civit Gartland...

50
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:12,125
The Five Dragoons, too.

51
00:04:14,041 --> 00:04:16,041
But there are only four of them.

52
00:04:16,166 --> 00:04:17,125
THE FIVE DRAGOONS
BLACK DRAGON KNIGHTS

53
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:19,041
THE FIVE DRAGOONS
BLACK DRAGON KNIGHTS
- There's one missing...

54
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:21,125
I sealed his lips, Orban.

55
00:04:21,125 --> 00:04:24,083
ORBAN
- Look, was there any need to kill him?

56
00:04:24,125 --> 00:04:27,166
You shouldn't get carried away
with side gigs either.

57
00:04:27,166 --> 00:04:30,041
I take it Ortola ordered this?

58
00:04:35,083 --> 00:04:37,166
Ah, Seras...

59
00:04:39,125 --> 00:04:44,041
Everything about you restored this old,

60
00:04:44,083 --> 00:04:47,125
withered ruler to
a man brimming with vigor.

61
00:04:50,125 --> 00:04:53,125
I don't begrudge letting you escape.

62
00:04:53,125 --> 00:04:55,208
I don't begrudge it, but...

63
00:04:58,166 --> 00:05:04,000
The thought of another man
one day defiling you...

64
00:05:04,041 --> 00:05:05,125
Oh, Seras!

65
00:05:05,125 --> 00:05:07,166
I'll pay as much money as it takes.

66
00:05:07,166 --> 00:05:11,083
And if I must offer anything else,
I will gladly do so.

67
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:13,041
So, please...

68
00:05:13,083 --> 00:05:16,166
Please die and vanish from this world!

69
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:19,083
Emperor Ortola... wants me...?

70
00:05:19,125 --> 00:05:21,208
Aw, now she's frozen up.

71
00:05:21,208 --> 00:05:22,208
Poor thing.

72
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,166
Gizun was going to be a
hindrance at this stage,

73
00:05:26,208 --> 00:05:28,125
therefore I killed him.

74
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:31,166
Had he dodged, however,
I would have let him live.

75
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,083
Gizun was paralyzed and unable to move,

76
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:36,041
but he couldn't have evaded that either way.

77
00:05:36,041 --> 00:05:38,166
How should we deal with Seras Ashrain?

78
00:05:39,041 --> 00:05:41,000
What did His Majesty say?

79
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,125
SCHWEITZ
VICE CAPTAIN OF THE BLACK DRAGON KNIGHTS
- That it was up to us.

80
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:44,208
What shall we do?

81
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,208
How about passing her around our subordinates
as a reward before we kill her?

82
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,208
That would cause issues, Schweitz.

83
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:56,000
The former holy emperor asked us to bring
her corpse back with her purity intact.

84
00:05:56,166 --> 00:05:59,166
Wh-What nonsense are you people spouting?!

85
00:05:59,166 --> 00:06:04,000
Apparently the geezer can't die
in peace so long as you're alive.

86
00:06:04,125 --> 00:06:06,083
Y-You lie...

87
00:06:08,083 --> 00:06:12,000
Seras Ashrain, I'll grant you
the right to win your life.

88
00:06:13,083 --> 00:06:14,041
The right?

89
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:19,208
Sir Civit is saying that if you duel him
and win, he'll let you go, Lady Seras.

90
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,083
MITAMA
- The Spirit Regalia of Holy Neah's
knight captain is renowned.

91
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:25,000
The Spirit Regalia of Holy Neah's
knight captain is renowned.

92
00:06:25,083 --> 00:06:28,208
I would be satisfied with the opportunity
to test your Spirit Regalia in battle...

93
00:06:28,208 --> 00:06:32,166
Or so I thought until just moments ago.

94
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:33,166
Sir Civit?

95
00:06:34,041 --> 00:06:38,041
I now find myself more interested
in this young man than Seras Ashrain.

96
00:06:38,083 --> 00:06:41,041
CIVIT GARTLAND
CAPTAIN OF THE BLACK DRAGON KNIGHTS
- Who might you be?

97
00:06:42,083 --> 00:06:45,208
I've got a knife to my throat...

98
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:48,166
But he's still out of range.

99
00:06:49,083 --> 00:06:50,125
Humanity's Strongest...

100
00:06:50,125 --> 00:06:52,041
Civit Gartland.

101
00:06:52,041 --> 00:06:54,125
A man more dangerous than the Soul Eater.

102
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,125
Why are you grinning?

103
00:06:58,125 --> 00:06:59,208
Ah, right.

104
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,125
Why is it that moments like this make me...

105
00:07:03,041 --> 00:07:05,041
Hey, Civit Gartland.

106
00:07:05,125 --> 00:07:07,125
Care to have a little chat?

107
00:07:09,041 --> 00:07:12,000
I would hear your name first.

108
00:07:12,125 --> 00:07:14,041
It's Hati Skoll.

109
00:07:14,083 --> 00:07:15,208
I see. An alias?

110
00:07:16,125 --> 00:07:17,166
Well, yeah.

111
00:07:17,208 --> 00:07:20,208
So you have a need to
conceal your real name.

112
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
I take it there's some history there.

113
00:07:23,125 --> 00:07:27,000
Sir Civit, why on earth are
you bothering with this boy?

114
00:07:27,041 --> 00:07:28,208
Don't you find it odd?

115
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,041
He stands before the Five Dragoons
but he's not frightened.

116
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:35,083
He's waiting for an opening
so he can attack.

117
00:07:35,125 --> 00:07:37,083
Attack you?

118
00:07:37,125 --> 00:07:41,208
He knows that one wrong move
will see him instantly slaughtered.

119
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:46,000
Yet even in such a situation,
he smiles and seeks conversation.

120
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,041
Huh.

121
00:07:47,041 --> 00:07:48,166
He's a clever man.

122
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:51,166
It's too early to close
the curtains on this stage.

123
00:07:52,041 --> 00:07:53,083
Don't get hasty.

124
00:07:53,083 --> 00:07:55,208
Make the wrong choices
and this is over in a flash.

125
00:07:56,125 --> 00:07:58,000
I'd like to ask you something.

126
00:07:58,083 --> 00:08:00,000
Very well. State your question.

127
00:08:00,125 --> 00:08:04,125
I gather you're searching for a foe
who can satisfy you.

128
00:08:04,125 --> 00:08:05,166
Indeed I am.

129
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:10,125
But aren't there plenty of strong, superhuman
opponents crawling around everywhere?

130
00:08:10,166 --> 00:08:12,166
For example, the goddess of Alion.

131
00:08:13,083 --> 00:08:17,125
My land of Bakoss and Alion
have forged close relations.

132
00:08:17,125 --> 00:08:18,125
However...

133
00:08:18,125 --> 00:08:22,125
I have high hopes for the heroes
she's summoned from another world.

134
00:08:22,208 --> 00:08:25,166
The power of her blessing grants
such heroes the ability

135
00:08:25,208 --> 00:08:28,083
to rapidly approach the peak of strength.

136
00:08:28,083 --> 00:08:31,041
I have faith that they will prove worthy
foes for me, and so I await that day.

137
00:08:31,083 --> 00:08:34,083
- I have faith that they will prove worthy
foes for me, and so I await that day.
- He's oozing with absolute self-confidence.

138
00:08:34,125 --> 00:08:37,166
His only desire is finding
and fighting powerful opponents.

139
00:08:38,083 --> 00:08:39,208
"Humanity's Strongest"
is too strong for his own good.

140
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,083
- "Humanity's Strongest"
is too strong for his own good.
- Seras Ashrain.

141
00:08:41,083 --> 00:08:43,166
- "Humanity's Strongest"
is too strong for his own good.
- I've lost interest in you at this point.

142
00:08:43,166 --> 00:08:46,041
I'll at least do you the honor
of delivering your head

143
00:08:46,041 --> 00:08:48,083
to Cattleya, the princess of Neah.

144
00:08:48,166 --> 00:08:50,041
You would do that to the princess?

145
00:08:50,083 --> 00:08:52,041
Silence, resigned weakling!

146
00:08:52,125 --> 00:08:57,083
You are the reason Bakoss
suddenly changed its stance

147
00:08:57,083 --> 00:09:00,125
and invaded Neah in the
first place, Seras Ashrain.

148
00:09:00,125 --> 00:09:01,083
What?!

149
00:09:01,125 --> 00:09:03,125
Why are you acting surprised?

150
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:05,208
You already had an inkling
of the truth, didn't you?

151
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,041
Bakoss wiped out Neah because

152
00:09:08,083 --> 00:09:10,208
our goddess demanded they
hand over their little paladin,

153
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,166
and your holy emperor refused.

154
00:09:13,166 --> 00:09:15,083
They reaped what they sowed.

155
00:09:15,125 --> 00:09:16,083
That can't be...

156
00:09:16,125 --> 00:09:20,125
Nothing kills my interest more than those who
refuse to struggle even in the face of death.

157
00:09:20,125 --> 00:09:23,041
Even if they're weak,
as long as they come at me...

158
00:09:23,041 --> 00:09:29,083
Though it goes without saying that I'd greatly
prefer it if they have the power to kill me.

159
00:09:30,125 --> 00:09:34,041
I've put together our path to survival now.

160
00:09:34,166 --> 00:09:36,083
Civit Gartland.

161
00:09:36,125 --> 00:09:39,166
You desire a foe who can
threaten your life, right?

162
00:09:40,041 --> 00:09:41,083
Indeed I do.

163
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:43,041
Then how about I become that for you?

164
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:48,125
You said those the goddess blesses
rapidly approach peak strength, right?

165
00:09:50,041 --> 00:09:52,083
Playing this card will
be our watershed moment.

166
00:09:53,083 --> 00:09:55,166
My real identity is Touka Mimori,

167
00:09:55,208 --> 00:09:57,041
a hero from another world.

168
00:09:59,125 --> 00:10:02,125
Sir Tooka... you're a
hero from another world?

169
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,208
Now the pieces click.

170
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,208
That's why something felt off.

171
00:10:07,208 --> 00:10:10,125
However, what are you doing
in a place like this?

172
00:10:10,125 --> 00:10:12,125
Civit is capable of sensing lies,

173
00:10:12,125 --> 00:10:14,166
so blatant falsehoods won't fly here.

174
00:10:14,208 --> 00:10:16,166
I hold a unique position,

175
00:10:16,208 --> 00:10:18,166
even among my fellow heroes.

176
00:10:18,208 --> 00:10:21,125
So I'm acting alone, independent of them,

177
00:10:21,125 --> 00:10:23,125
all at the goddess's behest.

178
00:10:23,166 --> 00:10:25,083
None of that was untrue.

179
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:26,083
It was all fact.

180
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:28,041
But Civit can interpret it as he will.

181
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:31,166
Why are you acting independent
of the other heroes?

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,041
Apparently, I'm in an altogether
different league than the rest.

183
00:10:35,166 --> 00:10:36,125
Oh?

184
00:10:36,125 --> 00:10:38,166
That's right. I'm an E-Class hero.

185
00:10:38,208 --> 00:10:41,000
We're not at all on the same level.

186
00:10:41,041 --> 00:10:43,208
Because of that, I was sent out on my own.

187
00:10:44,083 --> 00:10:47,000
A man even the goddess
recognizes as special, huh?

188
00:10:47,041 --> 00:10:50,208
Yeah. Seems I'm really quite special to her.

189
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,125
Now this is interesting.

190
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:56,125
So, hero from another world,
what is it you'd ask of me?

191
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Deferment.

192
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,083
You want me to spare you for now?

193
00:11:00,083 --> 00:11:02,000
What's in it for me?

194
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,166
I'll grow stronger than I am now
and then kill you.

195
00:11:05,041 --> 00:11:07,125
You say you'll kill me?

196
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:11,000
I'll grow stronger than
anyone or anything else.

197
00:11:11,041 --> 00:11:14,125
I'm going to gain enough power
to trample that goddess!

198
00:11:15,083 --> 00:11:16,208
Then let me ask you this.

199
00:11:16,208 --> 00:11:18,208
How do you plan to grow so strong?

200
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,166
I'm headed to the Land
of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

201
00:11:22,041 --> 00:11:26,000
I'm walking a different path
than the other heroes.

202
00:11:26,083 --> 00:11:30,041
The Goddess Vicius
has granted me that freedom.

203
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:34,166
If they survive the ruins and reach
the surface, we interfere no more.

204
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:36,208
Alion grants that person
the right to live freely.

205
00:11:37,041 --> 00:11:39,208
Either way, I plan to return to her.

206
00:11:40,083 --> 00:11:43,041
So you're saying there's no
chance you'll just disappear.

207
00:11:43,041 --> 00:11:44,125
No way in hell.

208
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,166
Indeed, I swear I'll make it back
to the goddess...

209
00:11:48,083 --> 00:11:50,083
To exact my revenge!

210
00:11:50,166 --> 00:11:51,208
Very well.

211
00:11:51,208 --> 00:11:53,083
I wish to see this.

212
00:11:53,083 --> 00:11:56,041
I want to see what becomes of your growth.

213
00:11:56,083 --> 00:11:58,125
Then I'd like us to fight to the death.

214
00:11:58,125 --> 00:12:00,083
Yeah, me too.

215
00:12:01,125 --> 00:12:06,208
So let's settle this just between
us one day, Civit Gartland!

216
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:10,125
How delightful!
That will to fight! That hostility!

217
00:12:10,166 --> 00:12:13,166
Very well! I shall let you live, Tooka Mimori!

218
00:12:14,083 --> 00:12:15,208
Now that's the spirit.

219
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,041
You may leave this place without worry.

220
00:12:18,083 --> 00:12:22,041
Once we have silenced Seras Ashrain,
then we shall leave as well.

221
00:12:22,041 --> 00:12:23,125
That won't do.

222
00:12:23,125 --> 00:12:27,125
I need Seras's power in order to make it
through the Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

223
00:12:27,125 --> 00:12:29,208
You'd take her with you
without the goddess's approval?

224
00:12:30,125 --> 00:12:31,208
That doesn't matter.

225
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,208
I'll use Seras Ashrain
to grow stronger for myself.

226
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,083
That's all there is to it.

227
00:12:41,166 --> 00:12:43,125
Good, Tooka Mimori!

228
00:12:43,125 --> 00:12:46,083
Then I suppose I shall grant
Seras Ashrain mercy as well.

229
00:12:46,083 --> 00:12:48,000
Wait, what?! Civit!

230
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,041
Tooka says he needs her to get stronger.

231
00:12:51,041 --> 00:12:54,041
We can always kill her
after his duel with me.

232
00:12:54,041 --> 00:12:55,083
Yeah, but even so...

233
00:12:55,125 --> 00:12:56,208
What if he disappears on you?

234
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Silence.

235
00:12:58,083 --> 00:12:59,083
Or I'll kill you!

236
00:13:02,083 --> 00:13:05,083
- Sir Tooka?
- Sorry, Seras, that's how it is.

237
00:13:05,125 --> 00:13:06,083
Schweitz.

238
00:13:06,083 --> 00:13:09,166
Tell Grimm Ritter as well,
wherever he's off wasting time.

239
00:13:09,166 --> 00:13:11,083
No one is to lay a hand on these two.

240
00:13:11,125 --> 00:13:12,125
Very well.

241
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,166
This first act proved to be a performance
that far surpassed my imagination.

242
00:13:17,208 --> 00:13:20,166
It was an excellent lead into the next.

243
00:13:20,208 --> 00:13:24,208
I look forward to the day when
we meet again, Tooka Mimori!

244
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,083
It worked.

245
00:13:26,166 --> 00:13:29,166
I managed to get Civit to let us go.

246
00:13:30,083 --> 00:13:31,125
And I won my gamble!

247
00:13:32,125 --> 00:13:33,083
Meaning...

248
00:13:33,208 --> 00:13:35,000
He's in range now!

249
00:13:35,208 --> 00:13:36,166
Para...

250
00:13:36,208 --> 00:13:38,166
Tooka!

251
00:13:38,208 --> 00:13:39,208
...lyze!

252
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,041
You bastard!

253
00:13:47,083 --> 00:13:50,125
I'm impressed, "Humanity's Strongest."

254
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:57,083
Sorry, but I have no intention of dragging
things out with you for that long.

255
00:13:57,208 --> 00:14:01,208
This isn't some nice little play,
Civit Gartland.

256
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:05,041
Why not? Because it's a tale of revenge.

257
00:14:05,166 --> 00:14:07,083
Looking at things logically,

258
00:14:07,125 --> 00:14:10,125
you Black Dragon Knights
are nothing but a liability for me.

259
00:14:11,083 --> 00:14:12,166
Therefore, you must be eliminated.

260
00:14:12,208 --> 00:14:14,000
There is no next act.

261
00:14:14,041 --> 00:14:18,083
What... have you done, Tooka?!

262
00:14:18,083 --> 00:14:22,166
Like I said, I'm putting a hard stop
to this little song and dance,

263
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:24,083
Black Dragon Knights!

264
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,083
Tooka...!

265
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,125
I told you, didn't I?

266
00:14:32,166 --> 00:14:34,166
I'm in a different league.

267
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:36,083
Poison.

268
00:14:46,208 --> 00:14:48,166
Tooka!

269
00:14:50,083 --> 00:14:53,166
They don't call him "Humanity's
Strongest" for nothing.

270
00:14:54,166 --> 00:14:58,125
This is the second time I've seen someone
force themself to move while paralyzed.

271
00:15:00,041 --> 00:15:02,166
But it's just suicide.

272
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:07,083
That was close.

273
00:15:10,083 --> 00:15:12,041
I've never seen anyone move so much

274
00:15:12,083 --> 00:15:14,166
after eating my Paralysis and Poison combo.

275
00:15:15,041 --> 00:15:18,083
I'll need to remain ready for
anything until I see him expire.

276
00:15:25,166 --> 00:15:28,125
A signal to a squad
on standby elsewhere, huh?

277
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,083
Sir Tooka.

278
00:15:32,166 --> 00:15:35,125
I'm staying here to see
the Five Dragoons dead.

279
00:15:35,125 --> 00:15:37,041
You're welcome to run if you want.

280
00:15:37,083 --> 00:15:38,208
I shall stay as well.

281
00:15:38,208 --> 00:15:41,125
I am currently your bodyguard, after all.

282
00:15:41,166 --> 00:15:45,125
Though in exchange, I will be accepting
those blue dragon gems as my reward.

283
00:15:45,125 --> 00:15:47,041
Yeah, got it.

284
00:15:51,041 --> 00:15:52,125
Sir Schweitz?!

285
00:15:52,166 --> 00:15:55,000
Wh-What happened to you?!

286
00:15:56,041 --> 00:15:58,125
- Azlan...
- S-Sir Civit!

287
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:00,125
- Y-You're actually wounded?!
- Kill them...

288
00:16:01,125 --> 00:16:03,041
from the sky!

289
00:16:03,166 --> 00:16:05,125
Don't get too close!

290
00:16:05,125 --> 00:16:08,000
Kill them at range!

291
00:16:08,041 --> 00:16:11,000
Kill those two no matter what!

292
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:11,208
We're linked.

293
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,208
There are two problems with this ability.

294
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,166
What are you doing?!

295
00:16:15,166 --> 00:16:16,166
Hurry!

296
00:16:16,208 --> 00:16:19,208
First is how long it takes
to enter this state.

297
00:16:20,125 --> 00:16:24,083
Second is how quick it burns
through my MP while it's active.

298
00:16:24,166 --> 00:16:25,125
In other words...

299
00:16:25,166 --> 00:16:28,041
this power we gained from the
monster enhancement solution

300
00:16:28,166 --> 00:16:30,041
is for super short combat!

301
00:16:30,208 --> 00:16:32,125
We're dropping them, Piggymaru!

302
00:16:33,125 --> 00:16:36,166
All right, let's settle this for good!

303
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:38,125
Assault Accel!

304
00:16:47,125 --> 00:16:48,083
Paralyze!

305
00:16:48,125 --> 00:16:51,166
Once we're linked, Piggymaru is half "me."

306
00:16:52,125 --> 00:16:55,041
So as long as we're connected like this,

307
00:16:55,041 --> 00:16:56,041
- Tooka!
- his farthest tendril
starts my effective range.

308
00:16:56,083 --> 00:16:57,041
- Sleep!
- his farthest tendril
starts my effective range.

309
00:16:57,083 --> 00:16:58,083
his farthest tendril
starts my effective range.

310
00:17:01,125 --> 00:17:03,125
Your skill has leveled up.

311
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,125
INFLICT FROZEN, INFLICT DARKNESS, INFLICT RAGE
- New skills have been unlocked.

312
00:17:06,125 --> 00:17:07,166
Berserk!

313
00:17:09,041 --> 00:17:13,083
This new Berserk skill probably
induces violent urges.

314
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:16,166
Combined with Paralyze,
it could kill an enemy quickly.

315
00:17:16,166 --> 00:17:18,166
Dismiss Paralyze and Sleep.

316
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Dark.

317
00:17:21,041 --> 00:17:23,125
Wh-What? M-My vision! I can't see!

318
00:17:23,166 --> 00:17:26,041
So this one obscures their eyes with darkness?

319
00:17:27,125 --> 00:17:30,125
Orban wanted to kill Seras for money.

320
00:17:30,166 --> 00:17:33,208
Schweitz wanted to use her
as a plaything for his men.

321
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:37,000
So using them as lab rats...
doesn't bother me at all.

322
00:17:37,125 --> 00:17:39,125
They're lowlifes, just like me.

323
00:17:39,125 --> 00:17:41,125
TOOKA MIMORI
- You have leveled up.

324
00:17:57,125 --> 00:17:58,208
It's quiet.

325
00:18:03,125 --> 00:18:04,125
Paralyze.

326
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:11,000
Tooka...

327
00:18:12,041 --> 00:18:16,041
You really are far too exceptional,
Civit Gartland.

328
00:18:16,125 --> 00:18:20,041
Just who the hell are you...?

329
00:18:20,083 --> 00:18:23,166
I'm nothing grand like a hero who
will save the world anymore.

330
00:18:23,208 --> 00:18:26,208
Now I'm just a simple avenger.

331
00:18:30,125 --> 00:18:33,000
So this is how Humanity's Strongest
meets his end, huh?

332
00:18:40,166 --> 00:18:43,166
Now we should be able to cover
Seras Ashrain's tracks.

333
00:18:43,208 --> 00:18:45,083
Thank you.

334
00:18:45,125 --> 00:18:47,083
I'm the one who should be thanking you.

335
00:18:47,125 --> 00:18:49,041
I was glad you stayed by me.

336
00:18:49,166 --> 00:18:52,083
I didn't think I could let you die.

337
00:18:53,083 --> 00:18:56,041
If I had let you fall here,

338
00:18:56,041 --> 00:18:58,125
I felt I would never recover this time.

339
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,083
I must say, Sir Tooka,
you're wearing a rather gentle expression.

340
00:19:03,166 --> 00:19:07,083
Maybe because I'm thinking of someone gentle.

341
00:19:07,166 --> 00:19:09,083
That aunt you mentioned?

342
00:19:15,041 --> 00:19:16,166
So, this Hero Slayer...

343
00:19:17,083 --> 00:19:20,125
He could potentially surpass
Humanity's Strongest one day.

344
00:19:20,166 --> 00:19:23,083
He's an aggressive, bloodthirsty man.

345
00:19:23,083 --> 00:19:24,125
What's the matter?

346
00:19:24,208 --> 00:19:27,083
The dragons that the Five Dragoons rode

347
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:29,125
were a different size than the others, right?

348
00:19:29,125 --> 00:19:31,083
What? O-Oh, yes.

349
00:19:31,083 --> 00:19:34,041
Then I think... I already crushed him.

350
00:19:34,041 --> 00:19:35,041
Huh?

351
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:43,083
You were even able to defeat
the Hero Slayer so easily?

352
00:19:43,208 --> 00:19:45,041
Apparently.

353
00:19:53,041 --> 00:19:54,125
TITLE: S-CLASS HERO
AYAKA SOGOU

354
00:19:54,125 --> 00:19:55,125
TITLE: S-CLASS HERO
AYAKA SOGOU
- I still haven't awakened a unique skill?

355
00:19:55,166 --> 00:19:56,125
I still haven't awakened a unique skill?

356
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:59,125
Huh? What's with this chick?

357
00:20:03,125 --> 00:20:04,166
NYANTAN KIKIPAT
FOLLOWER OF VICIUS

358
00:20:04,208 --> 00:20:05,208
NYANTAN KIKIPAT
FOLLOWER OF VICIUS
- I'm here on behalf of the Goddess Vicius.

359
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,041
I'm here on behalf of the Goddess Vicius.

360
00:20:07,083 --> 00:20:10,083
Henceforth, when she is preoccupied, I shallâ€”

361
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:12,208
A skinny shrimp like you
is gonna boss us around?

362
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,125
I mean, are you any stronger than we are?

363
00:20:15,125 --> 00:20:17,083
You must be Oyamada.

364
00:20:17,166 --> 00:20:21,041
Your foul mouth is indeed
enough to furrow one's brow.

365
00:20:21,041 --> 00:20:23,000
Would you care to find out?

366
00:20:27,125 --> 00:20:29,000
What?

367
00:20:29,041 --> 00:20:30,166
Damn... it...

368
00:20:32,208 --> 00:20:34,125
I don't believe it!

369
00:20:34,166 --> 00:20:36,083
How can she be so fast?

370
00:20:36,125 --> 00:20:39,083
I hope that will suffice as an introduction.

371
00:20:39,125 --> 00:20:41,000
We're returning to the royal capital.

372
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,208
You all are to enter the next stage soon.

373
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,125
I see.

374
00:20:47,125 --> 00:20:49,208
Nothing to be proud of, you see.

375
00:20:50,125 --> 00:20:54,166
Still, I'll use my judgment and mercilessly
trample any obstacle to my revenge.

376
00:20:55,041 --> 00:21:01,041
I can't say I don't have my own thoughts
and feelings about the goddess of Alion now.

377
00:21:01,083 --> 00:21:06,166
So please make good use of my strength
in the name of your revenge.

378
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,083
This is just a selfish quest for vengeance.

379
00:21:11,208 --> 00:21:13,083
I hardly see any of the righteousness

380
00:21:13,125 --> 00:21:15,083
or honor and conviction
that you value in it.

381
00:21:15,125 --> 00:21:21,083
No, you risked your life without any regard
for the dangers involved in order to save me.

382
00:21:21,166 --> 00:21:23,166
I want to repay that debt.

383
00:21:23,208 --> 00:21:25,125
As long as you believe it is right,

384
00:21:25,125 --> 00:21:28,000
I will happily accept any treatment.

385
00:21:28,041 --> 00:21:30,166
If you're that insistent,
then do as you please.

386
00:21:30,166 --> 00:21:32,041
Thank you very much.

387
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:36,083
Can I rely on your strength, Seras Ashrain?

388
00:21:36,083 --> 00:21:39,125
I promise to live up to your expectations.

389
00:21:40,125 --> 00:21:42,125
I'm sorry, Seras.

390
00:21:44,166 --> 00:21:46,041
Sir Tooka?

391
00:21:46,125 --> 00:21:51,083
I plan to return the favor
to you one day as well.

392
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,125
I always repay my debts,

393
00:21:53,125 --> 00:21:55,000
be it out of gratitude...

394
00:21:55,125 --> 00:21:57,083
or out of spite.

395
00:23:30,208 --> 00:23:32,166
Good work today.

396
00:23:33,166 --> 00:23:38,166
I knew I was right to ask you
to watch over the heroes.

397
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,208
You're strong, and you're wise.

398
00:23:41,208 --> 00:23:44,125
And above all, you're loyal.

399
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,083
Isn't that right, Nyantan?

400
00:23:47,166 --> 00:23:48,166
Yes.

401
00:23:48,208 --> 00:23:50,166
My, my, what's the matter?

402
00:23:50,208 --> 00:23:53,041
It feels like your mouth isn't moving.

403
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:00,083
Thank you very much for the
unchanging display of loyalty.

404
00:24:03,041 --> 00:24:06,208
The day the heroes clash with the
forces of the Great Demon Empire

405
00:24:06,208 --> 00:24:09,125
might be getting surprisingly close.

406
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
MONROY'S BLOODSPORT CHAMPION

